# =============================================================================
# EXCEPTIONS (Files to track)
# =============================================================================

# Keep essential empty directories
!data/.gitkeep
!outputs/.gitkeep  
!artifacts/.gitkeep
!logs/.gitkeep

# Keep configuration examples
!.env.example

# Keep test data
!tests/data/
!tests/fixtures/

# Keep the Phase-30 frozen gold fixture (D30-06).
#
# The two entries above are DIRECTORY patterns -- a trailing-slash pattern matches the
# directory, NOT the files inside it -- so neither re-includes a parquet. The blanket
# `*.parquet` rule in the PROJECT SPECIFIC block above (line ~252) therefore still wins for
# tests/fixtures/gold/*.parquet, and `git add` on those paths would silently no-op.
#
# tests/fixtures/gold/ holds the pre-Phase-30 ATS gold matrix and its closing-odds slice,
# frozen so the four Phase-29 harness reproductions in
# tests/unit/test_line_movement_readout_md.py keep proving the published numbers came from
# the committed harness even after Phase 30 rebuilds gold. Without this file-level negation
# the fixture is never committed and those reproductions pass only on the author's machine.
# This is deliberately NARROW: it re-includes parquets under tests/fixtures/gold/ ONLY, and
# leaves `data/` and every other parquet ignored.
!tests/fixtures/gold/*.parquet

# Keep documentation
!docs/
!*.md
!*.rst

# =============================================================================
# GRAPHIFY (personal knowledge-graph tool -- generated output + config)
# =============================================================================
# Placed AFTER the !*.md / !*.rst re-include block so they win (gitignore is
# last-match-wins): otherwise the blanket !*.md would re-track
# graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md.
graphify-out/
.graphifyignore
# Plan 31-11: the upstream pin's PROVENANCE RECORD. The `*.json` rule in the PROJECT
# SPECIFIC block above (line ~254) is what keeps every generated JSON out of history, and
# it catches this file too -- which would leave the pin's digests recorded ONLY inside the
# gitignored data/ tree, i.e. nowhere a fresh checkout can read them.
#
# config/upstream_pin.json names the exact nflverse snapshot every gold column and every
# gate baseline figure was measured against: source, nflreadpy version, UTC capture time
# and a sha256 for each of the 76 pinned season files under data/bronze/. The parquet
# stays ignored; the record does not. That asymmetry is the whole reproducibility claim --
# a checkout without the bytes can still say WHICH bytes were used, and can detect that
# what it has is not them.
#
# Deliberately NARROW: it re-includes this one file, and leaves every other JSON ignored.
!config/upstream_pin.json

# Phase 32 (CR-01/CR-02 of the 32-REVIEW): the LIVE zone's committed capture record, one
# file per live season. The same `*.json` rule at line ~254 that swallowed
# config/upstream_pin.json above swallows this directory too --
# `git check-ignore -v config/upstream_live/2027.json` reported `.gitignore:254:*.json`.
#
# config/upstream_live/2026.json is in `git ls-files` ONLY because it was force-added.
# Tracking is a property of the INDEX, not of the path, so every FUTURE season's manifest
# was still ignored: 2027.json at the season roll, and any <season>.json recreated on a
# checkout where it had ever been removed. `git add config/upstream_live/` would silently
# skip it and `git status` would not show it -- the committed half of the reproducibility
# claim simply would not exist, with no error anywhere. That silent shape is the failure
# this phase is built to prevent.
#
# Same asymmetry as config/upstream_pin.json -- the parquet under data/bronze/ stays
# ignored, the record of WHICH upstream revision a verdict was measured against does not
# -- but this is a DIRECTORY that grows a new file every season, so a force-add covers
# only the season somebody remembered to force-add.
#
# Deliberately NARROW: one glob over one directory, and every other JSON stays ignored.
!config/upstream_live/*.json

# Local scratch for AI-assisted work: superpowers plan ledgers and Playwright screenshots.
.superpowers/
.playwright-mcp/
